Vita: game ticks at a fixed 30 Hz without frame interpolation, so the game keeps its real speed
when frames take longer than 33 ms (today ticks equal presented frames: 20 FPS is 2/3 speed).
Upstream's separate-tick path (the time-scale path, painting skipped inside ticks) runs at most N
ticks per loop (dusk_vita_fixed_ticks), drops any backlog beyond that instead of catching up, runs
one tick after a long gap instead of none, and keeps the frame limiter (video.maxFrameRate).
A loop that finds no tick due but one due within 4 ms (the limiter wakes a little early) waits
for it and runs it instead of painting the same frame twice, and the limiter adds that wait to
the frame so the loop stays in step with the ticks.
Off (0) unless the Vita entry turns it on; interpolation, when chosen, keeps upstream behaviour.

